    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so you're saying that when a neighborhood transitions from a historically established demographic to a newer, more diverse one, it's actually a higher risk for us to lend to businesses there? wouldn't a more diverse customer base actually be a good thing for growth? it feels like you're saying certain types of \"new\" communities are inherently less stable for banking.",
